\
## Hayes / exception tests\
\
`FROMLIB FLOAD HayesTest/HayesTest.fth` runs `exceptiontest.fth`, which assumes:\
\
| Expectation | 64Forth |\
|-------------|---------|\
| `ABORT` \uc0\u8594  CATCH code **-1** | Yes (`-1 THROW`) |\
| `ABORT"` \uc0\u8594  CATCH code **-2** | Yes (`-2 THROW`) |\
| Undefined via nested `EVALUATE` \uc0\u8594  **-13** | Yes when CATCH is active |\
\
Driver: `Resources/Library/HayesTest/`; expect `EERRORS @ = 0` in the summary.\
\
---\
\
## Gaps / optional future work\
\
1. Map data-stack under/overflow to **-3** / **-4** when a CATCH frame is active (still print message when uncaught).\
2. Map division-by-zero to **-9** (check before `sdiv` or trap).\
3. Map memory faults to **-7** via THROW when CATCH active.\
4. Map float stack faults to **-3/-4** or ANS **-60\'96-65** if desired.\
5. Optional **`.ERROR` ( n -- )** helper for spaced standard messages after `CATCH` (not required by ANS; useful for apps).\
\
None of these are required for the current Hayes exception subset green on 64Forth v0.8.\
\
---\
\
## Implementation map (kernel)\
\
| Piece | Location |\
|-------|----------|\
| `CATCH` / `(CATCH-OK)` / `THROW` | `forth.s` `XCATCH`, `XCATCH_OK`, `XTHROW` |\
| Uncaught THROW soft path | `_throw_abort` \uc0\u8594  message + `_error_abandon` |\
| Undefined word | `_undefined_word` (-13 if handler, else print + abandon) |\
| Compile-only | High-level `?COMP` \uc0\u8594  `-14 THROW` |\
| `ABORT` / `ABORT"` | `forth_init_str` colon definitions |\
| Soft abandon | `_error_abandon` |\
| Handler cell | `throw_handler` |\
